WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.833
Alice followed the Queen back to the croquet game.

2
00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:07.330
The players were taking a break and resting in the shade.

3
00:00:07.331 --> 00:00:11.578
As soon as they spotted the Queen, they leaped to their feet.

4
00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:17.058
"Why were you lying down, you lazy things?" the Queen demanded.

5
00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:19.626
"Start playing again at once.

6
00:00:19.627 --> 00:00:25.130
I'm warning you: A moment's delay will cost you your life!"

7
00:00:25.131 --> 00:00:31.799
The players quickly followed the Queen's orders, but she still wasn't happy.

8
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.521
She kept shouting, "Off with his head! Off with her head!"

9
00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:42.774
Every time the Queen shouted, a soldier took someone to prison.

10
00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:46.021
"The prison must be filling up," Alice thought.

11
00:00:46.022 --> 00:00:48.750
"And we're losing wickets again too."

12
00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:53.983
The soldiers had to stop being the wickets to follow the Queen's orders.

13
00:00:53.984 --> 00:00:58.881
Soon there were no wickets, and all the players were in jail.

14
00:00:58.882 --> 00:01:03.325
That is, all the players except the King, the Queen, and Alice.

15
00:01:03.326 --> 00:01:08.817
"There's nobody left for her to punish except the King and me!" Alice thought.

16
00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:12.274
But the Queen had finished sentencing people to death.

17
00:01:12.275 --> 00:01:16.299
Out of breath, she turned to Alice.

18
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:21.429
"Have you seen the Mock Turtle today?" the Queen asked.

19
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:25.097
"I've never seen one in my life," Alice said.

20
00:01:25.098 --> 00:01:27.489
"Come with me," the Queen said.

21
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:35.147
"We'll find him, and he'll tell you his story."

22
00:01:35.148 --> 00:01:39.494
As they walked away, Alice heard the King talking to himself.

23
00:01:39.495 --> 00:01:45.104
"I'm going to the prison to pardon everyone," he said.

24
00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:50.801
"Well, that's good," Alice thought.

25
00:01:50.802 --> 00:01:56.549
Alice and the Queen soon saw a strange winged creature sleeping in the sun.

26
00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:01.612
The animal had the head and wings of an eagle and the body of a lion.

27
00:02:01.613 --> 00:02:04.857
"Oh, that's a gryphon!" Alice exclaimed.

28
00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.689
"I never thought I'd see one in real life."

29
00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:10.372
The creature moved but didn't wake up.

30
00:02:10.373 --> 00:02:12.621
The Queen took care of that.

31
00:02:12.622 --> 00:02:16.206
"Get up right now!" the Queen bellowed.

32
00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:20.926
"Take this young lady to see the Mock Turtle and hear his story.

33
00:02:20.927 --> 00:02:26.327
I must go and check on my prisoners."

34
00:02:26.328 --> 00:02:32.021
As the Queen walked away, the Gryphon sat up and rubbed his eyes.

35
00:02:32.022 --> 00:02:35.833
He watched the Queen until she was out of sight.

36
00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:39.236
Alice was a little afraid of this odd animal.

37
00:02:39.237 --> 00:02:43.428
"But I guess I'm safer with him than with the Queen," she thought.

38
00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:50.452
"The Queen is always so amusing," the Gryphon said as he got to his feet.

39
00:02:50.453 --> 00:02:54.373
"The Executioner never cuts off anyone's head, you know.

40
00:02:54.374 --> 00:03:00.287
It's all in her imagination. Let's go."

41
00:03:00.288 --> 00:03:04.750
Alice was glad that no one was ever put to death.

42
00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:11.271
But she was annoyed that yet another creature was telling her what to do.

43
00:03:11.272 --> 00:03:16.507
They had not walked far before they spotted the Mock Turtle, sitting on a rock.

44
00:03:16.508 --> 00:03:22.768
As they approached, Alice could hear him sighing and sobbing.

45
00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.641
"What's wrong with him?" Alice whispered.

46
00:03:25.642 --> 00:03:32.164
"Nothing," the Gryphon said. "His problems are all in his imagination."

47
00:03:32.165 --> 00:03:36.583
The Mock Turtle looked at them with eyes full of tears.

48
00:03:36.584 --> 00:03:41.602
"This young lady wants to know your story," the Gryphon said.

49
00:03:41.603 --> 00:03:49.332
The Mock Turtle nodded. "Sit down, and don't say a word until I've finished."

50
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:52.586
So Alice and the Gryphon sat down.

51
00:03:52.587 --> 00:03:57.699
They waited and waited for the Mock Turtle to speak.

52
00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:03.668
"If he's ever going to finish, he needs to begin," Alice thought.

53
00:04:03.669 --> 00:04:10.616
At last the Mock Turtle started his story, which was mostly about his lessons at school.

54
00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:14.510
Once he began, he went on and on.

55
00:04:14.511 --> 00:04:20.355
"That's enough about lessons," the Gryphon finally interrupted in a firm voice.

56
00:04:20.356 --> 00:04:26.404
"Tell Alice about the lobster dance."

